.TH FALSE 1 "" "" "mcos Manual"
.SH NAME
false \- do nothing, unsuccessfully
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B false
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B false
does nothing and exits with a status of 1.
Arguments are ignored.
.PP
The shell has
.B false
built in as well; this program is what runs when it is called by path
(\fB/bin/false\fR) or from another program.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Always 1.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR true (1),
.BR sh (1)
